## Field dictionary

Use structured fields. Do not dump the same fact in three places.

**Identity**

- **Name**, **Acronym**, **Slug**, **Discipline** (specific profession: `vision rehabilitation`, `orthodontic technology`). Do not add another Sector option for a niche.
- **Sector**: prefer coarse tags already on the schema (`Health`, `Legal`, `Education`…). Existing niche tags may stay; do not grow the list.
- **Org type**, **Geography**, **Website**

**Standing**

- **Standing gate**: Membership standing | Register standing | Accreditation track | Programme only | Statutory only | None | Unknown
- **Continuing education required**: Yes only when the gate is membership, register, or accreditation. Programme-only and statutory-only → No, with the hours still recorded in **CE requirement**.
- **CE requirement**: short fact, e.g. `250 hours / 5 years (UKCP)` or `36 hours / year (AMA only)`
- **Standing complexity**, **Public register**

**Size and ops**

- **Members estimate** (number), **Members band** (must match the estimate), **Count year** (calendar year of that estimate; empty if unpublished), **Established year**
- **Admin model**, **Governance**, **Legal / charity no.** (format `Co 09179719` or `Charity 1150137`)
- **Membership system** is the *class*. Put the product name in **AMS product** (`Wild Apricot`, `MemberMojo`). Wild Apricot uses class `MemberMojo / lightweight` — do not rename that option (it would orphan existing rows).

**Contacts**

- **Primary email**, **Secondary email**, **Phone**, **Postal address**
- **Named contact** + **Contact role** (person if known)
- **Contact notes**: leftovers only — never repeat emails, phones, or company numbers already in typed fields

**Evidence**

- **Sources**: URLs only, one per line or separated by ` ; `
- **Tech signals**: one line of system evidence
- **Evidence confidence**: High = primary pages + a legal/register source; Medium = site only; Low = list mention or dead site
- **Research status**: Stub (name only) | Researched (fields + short body) | Deepened (standing gate evidenced)
- **Last researched**: the day you checked

**Pipeline**

- **Wave**, component scores, **Score breakdown**, **Score notes**, **Send rank**. Do not write **Fit score**.
- **Outreach status**, **Survey status**, **Survey response summary** (Surveyor/Tally later — do not invent values)
- **Opted out** / **Opted out on**: set when they say stop
- **Exclude reason**: one sentence, enough that the next agent does not re-open the case

**Marketing (fill on every Core Active)**

- **ICP lane**: Core = Active **and** the standing pain is likely still manual (volunteer or mix admin; manual / CMS / lightweight AMS; gated population is the membership or register product). Adjacent = Active but staffed mid-size, Known AMS, custom portal, or an accreditation track on a larger membership. Out = Backlog or Exclude. Active Wave + Adjacent lane is allowed — Wave is eligibility, lane is send priority.
- **Persona**: Secretary | Registrar | CEO / Director | Volunteer admin | Unknown
- **Lead source**: PSA register | HMRC List 3 | Peer of existing | Web search | Regulator site | Other
- **Next action**: Research | Draft survey email | Send survey | Follow up | Pause | Done
- **Campaign**: Survey wave 1 (sendable Core) | Later | Not queued
- **Email angle**: Spreadsheets | Lightweight AMS | Volunteer admin | Register audit | Fees | Unknown
- **Outreach hook**: one sentence Mark can paste; no “CPD”
- **Pain hypothesis**: standing + fees + membership admin friction
- **Why now**: timing, not a second hook
- **Survey URL**: `https://research.goodstanding.co.uk/r/Bz5oLN?ref={slug}` for sendable Actives only
- **Preferred channel**, **Warmth** (Cold until they reply), **Owner** (Mark)
- **PSA accredited**, **Standing audit**, **Fee collection**, **Annual fee**, **Renewal month**
- **Member count source**: where the estimate came from
- **Companies House URL**, **LinkedIn**, **Follow-up on**, **Last contacted**
- **Cluster**: PSA small register | Complementary | Animal | Celebrant / funeral | Land / conservation | Editing / finance | Counselling | Specialist health | Trade / guild | ADR / mediation | Other. Use this for campaign batches, not another Sector tag.
- **Gated headcount**: number of people actually subject to the standing gate (accredited grades, endorsed trainers, registrants). Score **Size** from the org Members band; use gated headcount to choose Core vs Adjacent and to write an honest hook. Empty if unpublished.
- **Sendable**: Yes only if Wave=Active, not opted out, not Stub, and Primary email is present. No email → Sendable No, even if Active.
- **Email quality**: Named person | Generic inbox | Unverified | None
- **CE policy URL** and **Register URL**: the one-click evidence links. Keep **Sources** as the full URL list.
- **Subject line**: survey email subject; no “CPD”
- **HQ town**: for later in-person clustering

Do not put “CPD” in Outreach hook, Pain hypothesis, Why now, Subject line, or Score notes.

## Page body template

Replace the whole body when cleaning a dumping-ground page. Do not append another spot-check heading.

```
## Purpose
One or two sentences.
## Establishment
Year, legal form, register status.
## Governance
Who runs it.
## Contacts
Only facts that are not already in properties, or a short named-person note.
## Website & systems
What the site is built on; whether CE is logged there.
## Fit notes
Wave + standing gate + why the score is what it is. One short deepen line if needed.
```

Never stack “spot-check — leave Exclude” sections. Update **Last researched** and **Exclude reason** instead.

## Research workflow

1. Follow this rule and fetch the database schema (do not assume property names).
2. Search name, acronym, and slug before creating (`notion-search` + `data_source_url`; no `filters.title_only`).
3. Read the body’s own membership, register, and continuing-education pages. Statutory regulator pages are supporting evidence, not a membership gate.
4. Fill structured fields first, then the short body.
5. Score from the table into the component number fields. Set Wave from the eligibility rules, not from the score. Do not write Fit score.
6. Unique slug. Recompute Send rank only if you can see the full sendable set. If you cannot see the full sendable set, leave Send rank empty. Do not invent ranks.
7. Fetch the page you just wrote and check: no duplicate emails in Contact notes; Sources are URLs; Score breakdown sums to Fit score; Stub has no Send rank.

## Parallel leftover hunting (coordinator + subagents)

Serial one-agent loops stall on output limits and duplicate uniqueness searches. Split the work: **hunt in parallel, create in series.**

Do **not** let two subagents create rows at the same time. Two uniqueness searches can both see empty and both create the same leftover.

### Coordinator (parent agent)

Owns Score audit, uniqueness lock, create, and reorient.

1. Query Score audit (`view://3d5ec775-22dd-8163-8e55-000ca563749b`). If it is not empty, finish those Actives first. Do not launch hunters.
2. Partition remaining official lists into **disjoint** name batches (no shared leftovers). Typical slices: HMRC List 3 complementary leftovers still unique; PSA complementary leftovers still unique; Charity Commission / OSCR / CCNI healer-association leftovers still unique; unpublished BAHA “40+” only if independently named with their own remaining-member hours.
3. Launch 2–4 hunter subagents in **one** turn. Each hunter gets: this Cursor rule, data source `9952bb13-ed3e-4c1f-8df5-6f65b98c4323`, the sit-on / already-slugged names **for its slice only**, and a hard **do not create / do not update CRM rows** rule.
4. Merge hunter packets. Drop already-slugged, sit-on, individuals, universities, Republic of Ireland-only, and statutory-only leftovers.
5. Coordinator uniqueness-searches the remaining names again.
6. Create **2–3 unique slugs** only (coordinator, or one creator subagent). `allow_async: true`, then poll. Re-query Score audit until empty. Recritical Fit / Wave / lane. Add a CRM field only if a real hole appears. Do not invent Send ranks. Campaign = Not queued on leftover creates.
7. Repeat until the remaining official lists are exhausted in Notion.

Coordinator replies stay short. Evidence lives in hunter packets and on the CRM pages, not in a growing uniqueness-closed dump in the parent transcript.

### Hunter subagents (parallel, read-only CRM)

Assigned one disjoint slice. Uniqueness-search each name (exact name, acronym, proposed slug). Read the body’s own membership / register / standing pages. Return a packet, then stop.

**Must not** create pages, update pages, or invent Send ranks.

Packet — one line per name, then a short Unique block only when needed:

- **Already slugged** — exact title + page id
- **Sit-on** — leftover name → existing slug (standing sits there)
- **Do not slug** — individual, university, venue, church-without-gate, statutory, no remaining-member body
- **Needs coordinator fetch** — search ambiguous; do not mark Unique
- **Unique, ready** — kebab slug; standing gate; Wave / ICP lane; Fit as `standing/size/systems/admin/contact`; official inbox or none; 3–8 source URLs; Distinct from…; Do not copy… (named-person / shared umbrella inboxes)

If uniqueness search is empty but the leftover is an absorbed / amalgamated / dissolved name that still appears on an official list, still return **Unique, ready** as Exclude so the next agent stops re-researching it.

### Creator subagent (one at a time)

Receives only Unique, ready packets the coordinator has re-checked. Creates those 2–3 rows. Does not hunt. Score checked = true. Last researched = today. Send rank empty. After create, the coordinator — not the creator — re-proves Score audit.

### Why create stays serial

Research of disjoint lists is embarrassingly parallel. Row creation is a uniqueness lock. Partition names; serialize create; parallelize hunting.

## Brand and copy

Internal research may quote a body’s own “CPD” scheme name in Sources or Exclude reason.

Do **not** put “CPD” in anything that could leak into survey or outreach copy (**Score notes**, page Fit notes, Survey response summary). Say continuing education, fees, membership, or good standing.

Do not invent Gmail files. Do not edit Tally from this workflow.

## Tooling limits

`query_data_sources` / AI search may be plan-gated. Fall back to `notion-search` scoped with `data_source_url` `collection://9952bb13-ed3e-4c1f-8df5-6f65b98c4323`, then `fetch` the page. Never create a row you could not uniqueness-check.

If Slack or a prior agent session is unavailable, treat this database as the source of truth.

## Confirmation boundaries

Ask Mark before: trashing pages; emailing anyone; changing Wave on a row already Sent or Engaged; collapsing Sector options in bulk; renaming `MemberMojo / lightweight`.

## Completion checks

- Unique slug
- Standing gate set
- Gated headcount filled when the gate applies to a known subset
- Count year filled when Members estimate has a dated source
- Fit score (formula) = sum in Score breakdown
- Send rank empty unless the row is sendable **and** the full set was recomputed
- Page body matches the template (no spot-check stack)
- Typed contact fields not repeated in Contact notes
